From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: gen1: fail the session open when the firmware
 rejects it

When the gen1 firmware cannot create a session, for example because its
session table is full (HFI_ERR_SYS_MAX_SESSIONS_REACHED), it answers
HFI_CMD_SYS_SESSION_INIT with a SESSION_INIT_DONE that carries the
error. The response handler only moves the instance to the error state,
and iris_hfi_gen1_session_open() still returns 0. The first REQBUFS
therefore succeeds, and the failure only shows up later as -EBUSY from
the next REQBUFS or from STREAMON, with nothing in the kernel log. A
client such as the Android Codec2 V4L2 HAL thus creates and configures
a component that can only fail once it is started.

After SESSION_INIT_DONE, return -EBUSY from the gen1 session open when
the instance is in the error state, so that the first REQBUFS fails
(iris_vb2_queue_setup() logs "session open failed" and returns
-EINVAL), and log the error code the firmware sent with
SESSION_INIT_DONE.

Sessions the firmware accepts are not affected. A rejected session
already stayed in the error state and every later REQBUFS or STREAMON
already failed with -EBUSY; only the point of failure moves to the
first REQBUFS. Closing a rejected session still sends SESSION_END, as
before.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c    | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 .../platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c   |  6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index 0e21b8eb92..d43b99bc90 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -130,7 +130,20 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_session_open(struct iris_inst *inst)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return iris_wait_for_session_response(inst, false);
+	ret = iris_wait_for_session_response(inst, false);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * A session the firmware cannot create, for example because its
+	 * session table is full, is answered with an error in SESSION_INIT_DONE,
+	 * and the response handler has moved the instance to the error state.
+	 * Fail the open instead of letting the client go on until STREAMON.
+	 */
+	if (inst->state == IRIS_INST_ERROR)
+		return -EBUSY;
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static void iris_hfi_gen1_packet_session_cmd(struct iris_inst *inst,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
index 0fa7967653..1fccb27ddc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_response.c
@@ -819,8 +819,12 @@ static void iris_hfi_gen1_handle_response(struct iris_core *core, void *response
 			struct hfi_msg_session_hdr_pkt *shdr;
 
 			shdr = (struct hfi_msg_session_hdr_pkt *)hdr;
-			if (shdr->error_type != HFI_ERR_NONE)
+			if (shdr->error_type != HFI_ERR_NONE) {
+				if (hdr->pkt_type == HFI_MSG_SYS_SESSION_INIT)
+					dev_err(dev, "session %#x: init failed, error %#x\n",
+						pkt->shdr.session_id, shdr->error_type);
 				iris_inst_change_state(inst, IRIS_INST_ERROR);
+			}
 
 			if (pkt_info->pkt == HFI_MSG_SESSION_FLUSH) {
 				if (!(--inst->flush_responses_pending))
